# Private GitHub Identity Workflow (Template)

Copy this file to `github-private-identity.mdc` locally and fill in your private values.

## Git (SSH) defaults
- Example only:
  - `git config --local core.sshCommand 'ssh -i ~/.ssh/<your_private_key> -o IdentitiesOnly=yes'`
  - `git remote set-url origin git@<your-github-host-alias>:<your-org-or-user>/<your-repo>.git`

## GitHub CLI defaults
- Example only:
  - `GH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/<your-gh-profile> gh ...`
  - `GH_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/<your-gh-profile> gh auth login -h github.com -p https -w`

## Notes
- Keep your real identity file outside git or ignored.
- Do not commit private usernames, host aliases, or local key paths.
